    echr:hasSupportingQuote "Social services drew up a welfare report on the applicant, noting on 23 July 2002 that he was suffering from schizophrenia, that he lived alone in a small, run-down annexe to his half-sister’s house and that his half-sister and his father’s second wife had stated that they did not wish to act as his guardian. The requirements for placement in a social care home were therefore deemed to be fulfilled"^^xsd:string,
        "and subsequently on 29 November 2005 by the Chief Public Prosecutor’s Office at the Supreme Court of Cassation."^^xsd:string ;
    echr:raisesArticle6Issue doc:issue_1 .

